Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1.3. Note on Conventions [run]", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.957512439635334*^9, 3.957512448754797*^9}, {
   3.979926544111343*^9, 3.9799265444353447`*^9}, {3.979926705353765*^9, 
   3.979926705473565*^9}, 
   3.9799890537205*^9},ExpressionUUID->"a4bd3bb0-e739-4fe4-ab34-b61c9a6a6450"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this code one is free to choose the sign of the Riemann ($RiemannSign=+1 \
for Wald, $RiemannSign=-1 for Rindler and Penrose). One also can choose the \
curvature spinors\[CloseCurlyQuote] sign with $PsiSign, $PhiSign, \
$LambdaSign. By default they are  +1, and in that case the Riemann tensor (in \
whatever convention you chose for its sign) is written in terms of the \
curvature spinors formally as in Rindler and Penrose\[CloseCurlyQuote]s book \
(use ",
 StyleBox["Decomposition[SP\[UnderBracket]RiemannCD[-A,-A\[Dagger],-B,-B\
\[Dagger],-C,-C\[Dagger],-D,-D\[Dagger]]] ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "to see this",
 "). If one then picks some of the $PsiSign, $PhiSign, $LambdaSign to be -1, \
then a minus sign appears in that expression that defines the curvature \
spinors. The GHP components of the curvature spinors are defined as the \
natural dyad components of the curvature spinors (use ",
 StyleBox["ToGHP[-,Dyad]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " to see this). Depending on our sign choices, GHP equations may look \
formally different than in other references, with minus signs involved in \
front of curvature GHP components. The same is true when one writes GHP \
curvature components in terms of the curvature tensors contracted with null \
frames (and notice the literature contains various typos there!). All of \
these can be checked using the built in expressions for decomposing the \
curvature tensors that the Spinors package includes, and on which SpinFrames \
operates, see Spinors documentation."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.957516483718096*^9, 3.957516585573454*^9}, {
   3.957516634135116*^9, 3.957516713010638*^9}, {3.95751676165952*^9, 
   3.957516769006577*^9}, {3.95751681831327*^9, 3.9575168422431097`*^9}, {
   3.957517668045233*^9, 3.9575177160159817`*^9}, {3.957517894272024*^9, 
   3.9575180174629498`*^9}, {3.957518195233118*^9, 3.957518195357442*^9}, {
